From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: the XP notification area's chevron button over its background

Purpose: the round blue arrow that shows the hidden notification icons.
Windows behavior: XP draws the arrow over the notification area's own
background, its corners show the notification area.
Wine before: after DrawThemeParentBackground, a themed push button with
transparent parts is filled with the brush of the parent's
WM_CTLCOLORBTN; the taskbar answers with the classic face colour, so the
arrow was on a beige square.
Change: in the XP shell, a push button whose parent is TrayNotifyWnd is
not filled after the parent's background, as the Start button already is
not.
Evidence: the button (class Button, BS_PUSHBUTTON, id 1502) of
TrayNotifyWnd showed a light face-coloured square around the arrow.
Scope: only the XP shell session and the notification area's buttons.
---
--- a/dlls/comctl32_v6/button.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32_v6/button.c
@@ -201,6 +201,18 @@
 
 typedef BOOL (*pfGetIdealSize)(BUTTON_INFO *infoPtr, SIZE *size);
 
+/* The XP notification area's button that shows or hides the inactive icons:
+ * XP draws its round arrow over the notification area's background, with no
+ * fill from the taskbar's WM_CTLCOLORBTN (the classic face colour). */
+static BOOL xp_tray_button(const BUTTON_INFO *info)
+{
+    WCHAR name[32];
+    HWND parent = GetParent(info->hwnd);
+
+    return COMCTL32_IsXPShell() && parent && GetClassNameW(parent, name, ARRAY_SIZE(name))
+           && !wcsicmp(name, L"TrayNotifyWnd");
+}
+
 static HTHEME start_button_theme(const BUTTON_INFO *info);
 static BOOL PB_GetIdealSize(BUTTON_INFO *infoPtr, SIZE *size);
 static BOOL CB_GetIdealSize(BUTTON_INFO *infoPtr, SIZE *size);
@@ -2929,7 +2941,7 @@
         /* Tests show that the brush from WM_CTLCOLORBTN is used for filling background after a
          * DrawThemeParentBackground() call. The XP taskbar answers with the classic face
          * brush, while XP keeps its themed background in the Start image's rounded corners. */
-        if (!external_start_button(infoPtr))
+        if (!external_start_button(infoPtr) && !xp_tray_button(infoPtr))
         {
             brush = (HBRUSH)SendMessageW(parent, WM_CTLCOLORBTN, (WPARAM)hDC, (LPARAM)infoPtr->hwnd);
             FillRect(hDC, &bgRect, brush ? brush : GetSysColorBrush(COLOR_BTNFACE));
